  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A quiet exhibition under lamplight",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"A quiet exhibition under lamplight\"**\n\nThe site is a personal, low-glare place to linger with art. The homepage frames actual collection cards on a dim wall and places volumes and collections on tactile shelves; the directory is a quieter finding aid. Both paths lead toward the artwork, never a dashboard of metrics. The published site and `PRODUCT.md` are the authority if this descriptive document drifts.\n\n**Key Characteristics:** image-first; warm but restrained; navigable like a book; visibly distinct treatment for photographed slabs versus reconstructed binder leaves; factual provenance and physical uncertainty available without pretending a catalogue image is an in-hand check.\n\nThe main layout is not an identical grid of cards. Homepage frames, shelf spines, directory rows, two-leaf desktop spreads, single-leaf mobile pages, and whole-slab viewing have different purposes. Do not force slabs into pockets or fabricate physical locations for the Trainer PDF-order sequence or top-loaded Trade cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "image-first",
      "warm but restrained",
      "navigable like a book",
      "visibly distinct treatment for photographed slabs versus reconstructed binder leaves",
      "factual provenance and physical uncertainty available without pretending a catalogue image is an in-hand check."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "Artwork Leads",
        "body": "Keep color on navigation and framing subordinate to actual local card and slab images. Do not use the foil sweep as gradient text.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "let the cards and whole slabs set the visual mood while chrome recedes.",
      "use manifest-backed physical order and distinguish owner-directed digital sequences from observed pocket placements in data and inspector.",
      "keep controls operable by keyboard and touch; check dark-background WCAG AA text contrast and multilingual glyphs at desktop and mobile widths.",
      "treat `PRODUCT.md` as the strategic brief, this file as a scan of real CSS, and `AGENTS.md` as the evidence and implementation rules."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "use generic SaaS / dashboard chrome: dark-blue uniform cards or a sticky app header.",
      "turn the site into TCG marketplaces (TCGPlayer, eBay): price tags, condition badges, buy buttons or listing-grid clutter. A handful of Trade cards does not change that rule.",
      "mimic crypto / NFT galleries with neon-on-black, glossy 3D or hype energy.",
      "make a corporate-minimal startup landing page: sterile white or stock-photo cleanliness.",
      "use gradient text, glassmorphism as a default, invented grades, owner status inferred from a reference print, or catalogue matches presented as in-hand identity checks."
    ]
  }
}
